	(text "U60 module notes: ESP32-C6-MINI-1 (PCB antenna).\n  Place at a board edge with the antenna end over\n  the board edge and keep copper, parts and the\n  HV/TIA area out of the antenna keep-out (MINI DS\n  v1.5 Fig 3-1 p10, Fig 11-1 p44; numeric\n  clearances UNRESOLVED, from the Hardware Design\n  Guidelines). The radio is not used."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 144.78 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b7904a5f-cfb9-4d64-8455-9ab5ffbda83c")
	)
	(text "Strapping (MINI DS Table 4-1/4-3 p12-13): GPIO9 high = SPI\n  boot; GPIO9 low with GPIO8 high = download boot. EN: 10k +\n  1u RC power-up delay (p40). GPIO15 left open (default\n  eFuses ignore it)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 139.7 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4c540981-7943-4bdc-8a36-fbb7d1b94b5a")
	)
	(text "DAC_HV safe default: MCP4728 EEPROM for channel C\n  is programmed to 0xFFF (lowest bias), VREF =\n  VDD, PD = 00, never power-down. HV_DIS (GPIO0,\n  pull-up on the Power sheet) gates the bias\n  regardless. UNRESOLVED until firmware exists."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 144.78 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ccb9093a-9663-43ed-bf4f-70d4d46f8516")
	)
	(text "Optional CAN bus ESD part: not fitted,\n  no part chosen (DNP footprint note\n  only)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 302.26 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "36a4b130-dddd-4207-ac13-31ef0e6ebfc0")
	)
	(text "DESIGN INTENT (Controller sheet, Rev A). Labels: VERIFIED = datasheet cited,\n  PROPOSED = design intent, UNRESOLVED = open. Nothing here is measured or\n  simulated.\nROLE (decision 11, PROPOSED): on-module ESP32-C6 supervises the analog chain. It\n  sets DAC_GAIN, DAC_TH, DAC_HV (MCP4728), reads HV_MON, VSPAN, VG, VMID\n  (ADS1115), gates the HV bias (HV_DIS), the comparator (SHDN_N) and hysteresis\n  (LE_HYS), reads LOS and PGOOD_VGA, and talks to the FPGA side over CAN\n  (CAN_H/CAN_L, 125 kbit/s). The analog path stays primary.\nWITHOUT FIRMWARE (PROPOSED): everything analog runs from its own references and\n  the Control sheet AGC; HV stays off (HV_DIS pull-up on the Power sheet); the\n  comparator stays enabled (SHDN_N pull-up on the Slicer sheet); HOLD_N is a\n  wire from the Connector.\nPIN MAP (module pad; research doc section 1): IO0 HV_DIS (Hi-Z at reset), IO1\n  SHDN_N, IO14 LE_HYS via R205 (DNP), IO2 SDA, IO3 SCL, IO6 LDAC, IO7 AUX via\n  R204, IO8 strap pull-up, IO9 BOOT, IO12/IO13 USB D-/D+, IO16/IO17 TXD0/RXD0\n  pads, IO18 CAN_TX, IO19 CAN_RX, IO20 LOS, IO21 PGOOD_VGA, IO22 DAC RDY, IO23\n  status LED. IO4, IO5, IO15 unconnected (no_connect).\nCHANGE FROM SPEC: IO10 and IO11 do not exist on the MINI-1 (MINI DS Table 3-1\n  p10-11; 22 GPIOs), so LDAC moved to IO6 and AUX to IO7 (JTAG MTCK/MTDO pins;\n  USB-Serial-JTAG is the debug path, so the external JTAG function is unused).\n  PROPOSED."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 12.7 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e82bead-c489-415a-a511-46b33fdcf716")
	)
	(text "STRAPPING (VERIFIED, MINI DS Table 4-1..4-3 p12-13): GPIO9 weak pull-up, high =\n  SPI boot; download boot needs GPIO8 = 1 and GPIO9 = 0 (BOOT pad to GND, then\n  EN pad). GPIO8 has R192 10k to 3V3_D. Do not drive IO8/IO9 at reset. IO0, IO1,\n  IO14 are Hi-Z at reset (C6 DS Table 2-2 p17-18), so the pull resistors on the\n  other sheets fix the safe state. IO18-IO23 have weak pull-ups at reset (CAN_TX\n  idles recessive).\nUSB (PROPOSED): J60 is for programming only. VBUS goes only to U61 pin 5 (not a\n  supply), CC1/CC2 5.1k to GND, D+/D- through R193/R194 (0R fitted, 22R\n  footprint, value UNRESOLVED). UART fallback on TP62/TP63.\nCAN (PROPOSED, research section 3): SN65HVD230 with RS = 10k to GND (slope\n  control, 80/120/160 ns edges, SLOS346O p8; 3 m leg passes the SLLA270 p9 stub\n  rule marginally). 125 kbit/s. NO termination on the module; one 120 ohm (or 2\n  x 60 ohm + 4.7 nF split, SLLA270 p8) at the FPGA-end junction only. Vref_OUT\n  unconnected."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 121.92 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "68e1a2ef-4454-41c8-a85e-e88c1cfc7d78")
	)
	(text "I2C (VERIFIED, MCP4728 DS22187E p21-24; ADS1115 SBAS444E p20): private bus,\n  MCP4728 at 0x60, ADS1115 ADDR = GND at 0x48. MCP4728 factory default is 0 V on\n  all channels (not Hi-Z). ADS1115 inputs must stay within GND-0.3 .. VDD+0.3 V;\n  all four sources are <= 3.3 V nodes. LDAC is held high by R197 so a high LDAC\n  keeps the EEPROM values on the outputs.\nUNRESOLVED: USB series resistor values; auto-reset behaviour over USB; DAC_GAIN\n  and DAC_TH safe direction; verification of the DAC_HV default after EEPROM\n  programming (General Call Read); measured 3V3_D current; antenna keep-out\n  numbers; -1 versus -1U module; VBUS back-feed against the 5 V cable rail."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 231.14 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4a923c6-4c66-4ee7-a2e0-30d53b0d7838")
	)
